        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61893012?u=7b888c8a0edaf519693218dd47152bb31950e425&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Description</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">This PR clarifies how a web developer can set up the web app manifest for their PWA to leverage getInstalledRelatedApps. This is done by providing an example of the PWAs self identifying related_applications manifest field with the required properties.</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Motivation</h3>\n\n<p dir=\"auto\">getInstalledRelatedApps for PWAs has recently shipped in desktop Chrome and Edge. This change will give web developers clarity on what is required of in the setup of their web app manifest to leverage this API.</p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/40658",
            "title": "Bring clarity to PWA manifest requirements needed to use getInstalledRelatedApps",
            "date_modified": "2025-08-20T11:40:52.000Z",
            "date_published": "2025-08-06T23:33:26.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "ishika-patel",
                "url": "https://github.com/ishika-patel"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/55398995?u=9f6a9837c9879eceb0abde487a338b92d4e206fc&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><p dir=\"auto\">Fox <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"2998825375\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/39152\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/content/issues/39152/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/39152\">#39152</a>. All the extra celebration was from when the editor itself would be printed, but that's no longer the case.</p>",
